Short:        C64, Plus/4, VIC-20 emulators 
Author:       krabobmkd
Uploader:     krabob@free.fr
Type:         misc/emu
Version:      3.10 r1
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.1
Requires:     OS3.1, 68060+, fast Amiga, MUI; optional: AHI, AmiSSLv5, RTG

---------------------------------------------------------------------------

KVICE 3.10 r1

---------------------------------------------------------------------------

WHAT IS IT?

KVICE is a Commodore 8-bit machine package for the classic Amiga:

  x64      Commodore 64 emulator
  xplus4   Commodore Plus/4, C16 and C116 emulator
  xvic     Commodore VIC-20 emulator
  PetMate  PETSCII art draw tool

It is a fork of VICE 3.10 (except for PetMate and PetMe), 
the Versatile Commodore Emulator, made fast for AmigaOS 3.x: 
Native scalable drawing in a window or fullscreen (RTG or 
native screens), MUI settings, AHI sound, joysticks and paddles, 
disk images, an Amiga drawer as drive 8, snapshots, 
BASIC programs saved/loaded as UTF-8 texts (.bas).

INSTALLATION

Double-click "Install". Then run "KVICE Resource Installer": the
resource files the emulators need are not in this archive, it
downloads and checks them.

REQUIREMENTS

  - AmigaOS 3.1 or later, 68060 or better
  - a fast Amiga for full speed:
      68060 50 MHz reaches 40% of the speed,
      Vampire, PiStorm and UAE reach 100% easily
  - MUI 3.8 or later, for the settings window
  - (optional) AHI, for the sound, else no sound
  - (optional) AmiSSLv5 and a TCP/IP stack, for online resource
    installation (KVICE Resource Installer)
  - (optional) RTG graphics

If you have no RTG extension and use Amiga native display modes, you are
encouraged to install the patch BlazeWCP from Aminet: it accelerates
the drawing function WriteChunkyPixels() by a large factor.

OK BUT THEN WHAT ?

 The first motivation to do another VICE port for Amiga was...
 I was never ever able to make any of the Official version work,
 nor find any documentation about why it wouldnt work. Infinite loop stuck issues.
 
 Then Well, I have a piStorm, I wanted my legitimate glorious C64 emulation to work.
 This version will boot if you have MUI in all case, then if ROMs or anywhat is
 missing, you'll have a report with clear message. If you have a Drive selected
 but its Drive ROM is missing, you will be clearly signified. 
 Yet if any file is missing you will be guided to a solution.
 
 I previously coded a PetMate PETSCII drawing tool for Amiga and needed to verify C64 
 integration of exports, so this PETSCII drawing tool is also provided here as option.

 Then I couldn't help doing nicer RTG rasterizer with scalable windows, optimize a bit, 
 and add a text export/import for BASIC as texts. And expose a few more
  d64 disk cool management functions. And fullscreen switch.
 
 So, as also the Amiga version was removed from official sources,
 this becomes officially "a fork" , named KVICE.
 Note it installs only "C64", "VIC-20" and "Plus4" emulators, when the
 original VICE 3.10 would install 11 emulators.

 You may install ROMs, that are not part of this project, from
 "C64 Forever" CD from Cloanto, or from anyone who claims to have the 
 rights to sell you this, at the moment you read this.

LICENSE

GPL 2 or later, like VICE. The PetMe fonts are under their own free
license (PetMe-FreeLicense.txt). The resource files that are not part of
KVICE have their own license terms.

